From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: Do not check github.com for updates by default

Codex is installed and updated by the package manager here, so the startup
update check is both useless and misleading: it queries
https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/releases/latest on every TUI start
and then offers an npm/brew/standalone upgrade action that cannot update an
RPM installation.  Flip the default to off; users who want it back can still
set check_for_update_on_startup = true in ~/.codex/config.toml.

Downstream-only distribution policy, not suitable for upstream submission.

--- a/codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs
@@ -3900,7 +3900,7 @@
 
         let review_model = override_review_model.or(cfg.review_model);
 
-        let check_for_update_on_startup = cfg.check_for_update_on_startup.unwrap_or(true);
+        let check_for_update_on_startup = cfg.check_for_update_on_startup.unwrap_or(false);
         let model_catalog = load_model_catalog(cfg.model_catalog_json.clone())?;
 
         let log_dir = cfg
